cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  paper it accompanies (see `preferred-citation`).
title: >-
  Trajectory analysis code for long-term NIR single-particle tracking with
  Au42 gold quantum needles
abstract: >-
  Analysis code accompanying the study of long-term near-infrared
  single-particle tracking with atomically precise gold quantum needles
  Au42(PET)32. Links per-frame TrackMate detections into trajectories using a
  displacement and intensity cost, and segments and classifies the motion of
  the tracked particle by DC-MSS (divide-and-conquer moment scaling spectrum),
  including the Monte-Carlo generation of the classification thresholds and a
  script that checks the results against the published values.
